{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>And you shall hold them as a possession for your children.</b> Take hold of them as a possession for the needs of your children after you. And it is not tenable to explain the bequeathing as being to your children — for if so, it should have written ״וְהִנְחַלְתֶּם״ them to your children; rather, וְהִתְנַחֲלְתֶּם is like וְהִתְחַזַּקְתֶּם." "<b>Each over his brother.</b> To include a prince over his people and a king over his officers — not to rule over them with rigor."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:29.593671128Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}